Package: bilatr
Title: Hierarchical Dynamic IRT Models for Latent Bilateral Relations
Version: 0.12.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("David", "Randahl", , "david.randahl@fhs.se", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Magnus", "Lundgren", role = "aut"),
    person("Carl", "Vikberg", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Estimates latent bilateral relations between pairs of
    actors over time with a hierarchical Bayesian dynamic
    item-response-theory-style model for dyadic event data. The latent
    scale runs from conflict to cooperation: it is oriented by a reference
    action type, so that with a cooperative reference higher values mean
    more cooperative relations. Users supply CAMEO-coded (or any
    categorically coded) dyadic event data in a documented, validated
    format; action types discriminate between more and less cooperative
    states through a Dirichlet-multinomial likelihood, and dyad-specific
    latent states follow a random-walk process, with support for both
    single-dyad time-series and multi-dyad panel estimation. Includes
    GDELT download/ingest helpers and a CAMEO recoding table,
    'cmdstanr'-based fitting wrappers, and tidy posterior extraction
    utilities.
